  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UEL- Minimiza negative env impacts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The implementation of this project aims to reduce the exploitation and use of non-renewable resources; instead, increase the efficiency of resource use through the use of alternative resources; reuse, recycle and recover materials in construction and landfill activities towards circular economy. For example, river sand is currently the main raw material used in construction and landfill activities, but this is a non-renewable resource. Given this situation, sea sand is considered an effective solution, asource of raw materials that can be used to replace river sand in construction and landfill activities. However, the characteristics of sea sand are that the grains are smaller and finer than river sand, resulting in poor load-bearing capacity, along withcontaining marine debris and high chloride content, leading to iron corrosion causing loss of structure during construction, not suitable for construction activities. However, in reality, many countries in the world such as China, Japan, the United States, Russia, Germany, Singapore, etc. have successfully applied sea sand processing technology for use in construction and landfill. Recently, to solve the problem of sandshortage in the construction of the North-South Expressway, Can Tho - Ca Mau section(under the North-South Expressway Construction Project, Can Tho - Ca Mau section), My Thuan Project Management Board has coordinated with the Institute of Transport Science and Technology to pilot the use of sea sand as roadbed material with a length of 300m, following the direction of the Ministry of Transport.</narrative>
  </description>
